    "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/CoE-Student-Engagement-Coordinator_JR0000996": {
      "title": "CoE Student Engagement Coordinator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nDepartment: College of Engineering Marketing Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: ●        A Resume ●        A Cover Letter For additional information please contact: Alaina Hill at Alaina.hill@oregonstate.edu This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a Criminal History Check and be determined to be position qualified as per OSU Standard 576-055-0000 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in Youth Programs may have additional Criminal History Checks every 2 years. This position requires driving a University vehicle or a personal vehicle on behalf of the University; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a Motor Vehicle History Check , possess and maintain a current, valid driver's license in their state of residence, be determined to be position qualified and self-report convictions (as per Voluntary and Compulsory Driver Standards OSU Standard 125-155-0200) as per OSU Standard 576-056-0000 et seq. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire.   Note: All job offers are contingent upon Human Resources final approval Job Description: This recruitment will be used to fill two part-time (a maximum of 24 hours per week) CoE Student Engagement Coordinator for the College of Engineering at Oregon State University (OSU). The College of Engineering (CoE) External Relations team is seeking an organized, detail-oriented student to join our team part-time (an average of 6-9 hours per week). This position supports both the College of Engineering Events and Donor Engagement programs, contributing to meaningful experiences for alumni, donors, students, faculty, and friends of the college. The Engagement Team Student Assistant will divide their time between event support and donor engagement activities. The position reports directly to the Associate Director of Events, who serves as the supervisor of record, while also providing regular support to the Associate Director of Donor Engagement. The student will work closely with both team members and will receive assignments and project direction based on operational needs. This role requires exceptional attention to detail, strong organizational skills, professionalism, and the ability to manage multiple projects effectively. Position Duties Data entry and maintaining event-related records and documentation Drafting event communications and documents Creating and printing name tags Delivering/picking up event equipment, materials or mail to COE event locations Editing, formatting, and preparing donor engagement materials and reports Printing, assembling, and mailing stewardship and donor communications Drafting stewardship materials such as impact pieces, thank-you notes, and related collateral Assisting with data analysis and reporting projects to improve stewardship efforts Transferable Skill Development OSU is committed to ensuring students are prepared for success after graduation through intentional skill development as student employees. The competencies students develop while working at OSU are defined by the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) as the essential skills employers seek in their hires. In this position, students learn and build vital career-readiness skills in the primary areas below:   Communication, Critical Thinking, Teamwork, Technology Qualifications: Full Employment Eligibility Requirements can be found here:   https://hr.oregonstate.edu/student-employment-manual/500-employment-eligibility-requirements Must be academically enrolled in a high school, community college, or university and pursuing a program or course of study Must meet Academic Standing Requirements; students on academic suspension are not eligible for employment Must meet the applicable minimal enrollment standard High School student: Regularly enrolled in a high school or participating in a home-schooling program Undergraduate and post-baccalaureate student: 6 credit hours per term Undergraduate international student: 12 credit hours per term* Graduate student officially admitted to Graduate School: 5 credit hours per term Graduate international student officially admitted to Graduate School: 9 credit hours per term* *International students may be allowed to carry fewer hours than specified above and still be considered “full-time” by the United States Citizenship and Immigration Services ( USCIS ). A reduced course load is approved by the   Office of International Services   ( OIS ), and must be provided to the Student Employment Center. Required Ability to work an average of 6-9 hours per week during the academic year, with occasional flexibility for special events in the office (Covell Hall) or at event spaces on campus. Availability during Fall, Winter, and Spring terms of the 2026-2027 school year unless otherwise discussed with hiring manager. Optional opportunity to work remotely approx. 3hrs per week in the summer. Ability to communicate in a professional, positive, and friendly manner. Experience in an office and/or event setting. Ability to lift up to 30 lbs. Experience with Microsoft Office Suite and/or Google Workspace. Strong organizational and time management skills. Exceptional attention to detail and accuracy. Ability to manage multiple priorities and projects simultaneously. Demonstrated commitment to promoting and enhancing diversity and inclusion. Able to maintain confidentiality. Ability to represent the College of Engineering with maturity and professionalism. Ability to work independently and collaboratively as part of a team. Responsible, dependable, punctual, and adaptable. This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a Criminal History Check and be determined to be position qualified as per OSU Standard 576-055-0000 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in Youth Programs may have additional Criminal History Checks every 2 years. This position requires driving a University vehicle or a personal vehicle on behalf of the University; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a Motor Vehicle History Check , possess and maintain a current, valid driver's license in their state of residence, be determined to be position qualified and self-report convictions (as per Voluntary and Compulsory Driver Standards OSU Standard 125-155-0200) as per OSU Standard 576-056-0000 et seq. Preferred Currently enrolled at Oregon State University. Experience handling sensitive/confidential information. Experience working in an office, customer service, event, or administrative environment. Working Conditions/Schedule: - Office, storage areas, events, work schedule will vary. - The Engagement Team Student Assistant works collaboratively with both the Events and Donor Engagement teams. - While the Associate Director of Events serves as the supervisor of record, the student will regularly support projects and assignments from both functional areas and is expected to communicate proactively with each supervisor regarding priorities, deadlines, and scheduling. Salary Range: Anticipated Start Date: 2026-09-18 Anticipated End Date:"
    },
    "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/CoE-Innovation-Labs-Student-Assistant--iLabs-_JR0000999-1": {
      "title": "CoE Innovation Labs Student Assistant (iLabs)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nDepartment: College of Engineering Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: ●        A Resume ●        A Cover Letter For additional information please contact: Erin McDowell at Erin.mcdowell@oregonstate.edu We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a Criminal History Check and be determined to be position qualified as per OSU Standard 576-055-0000 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in Youth Programs may have additional Criminal History Checks every 2 years. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire.   Note: All job offers are contingent upon Human Resources final approval Job Description: This recruitment will be used to fill 4 part-time (a maximum of 24 hours per week) Innovation Labs Students for the College of Engineering at Oregon State University (OSU). Position Duties The CoE Innovation Labs Student Technical Assistant responsibilities include: Operate , calibrate, and maintain machines, equipment, and tools. Consult with full time staff to diagnose existing problems, and assist in the generation of new solutions as appropriate. Under the guidance and advice of full-time staff, develop and apply creative engineering solutions intended to facilitate improved shop operations and maintain a safe, functional working environment. Advise iLabs users, build connections with peers and other user groups, and improve user experience through the application of thoughtful advice. Direct users toward appropriate solution(s) while maintaining a respectful and empowering environment. Support full-time Machinists with research prototyping and production jobs, implementing strategies and techniques developed via trainings and co-work with other staff. Cooperate with full-time staff and other student workers to develop and implement shop layout and organizational solutions. Assist with relocation of large machines, equipment, and materials, both manually and with mechanical assistance. Perform duties and tasks in support of the College of Engineering and its facilities, under guidance from iLabs and/or College of Engineering Facilities staff. Transferable Skill Development OSU is committed to ensuring students are prepared for success after graduation through intentional skill development as student employees. The competencies students develop while working at OSU are defined by the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) as the essential skills employers seek in their hires. In this position, students learn and build vital career-readiness skills in the primary areas below:   Communication, Critical Thinking, Teamwork, Technology, Leadership, Professionalism Qualifications: Full Employment Eligibility Requirements can be found here:   https://hr.oregonstate.edu/student-employment-manual/500-employment-eligibility-requirements Must be academically enrolled in a high school, community college, or university and pursuing a program or course of study Must meet Academic Standing Requirements; students on academic suspension are not eligible for employment Must meet the applicable minimal enrollment standard High School student: Regularly enrolled in a high school or participating in a home-schooling program Undergraduate and post-baccalaureate student: 6 credit hours per term Undergraduate international student: 12 credit hours per term* Graduate student officially admitted to Graduate School: 5 credit hours per term Graduate international student officially admitted to Graduate School: 9 credit hours per term* *International students may be allowed to carry fewer hours than specified above and still be considered “full-time” by the United States Citizenship and Immigration Services ( USCIS ). A reduced course load is approved by the   Office of International Services   ( OIS ), and must be provided to the Student Employment Center. Required Demonstrated ability to safely work in a shop environment or similarly hazardous workspace. Experience or significant interest in manual and computer-driven manufacturing processes. Experience or significant interest in designing products and/or engineering solutions. This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a Criminal History Check and be determined to be position qualified as per OSU Standard 576-055-0000 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in Youth Programs may have additional Criminal History Checks every 2 years. Preferred 1+ year of experience in CNC machining or CNC related coursework and/or work experience. 1+ year of experience in product design using CAD software, and/or experience programming CNC toolpaths using CAM software. 1+ year of experience with lathes, mills, or similar. Experience with woodworking and/or metalworking tools. Working Conditions/Schedule: Work to be performed in Innovation Labs located in Rogers, Merryfield, and Graf Halls. Salary Range: Anticipated Start Date: 2026-09-18 Anticipated End Date:"
    },
    "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Annual-Giving---Gift-Planning-Engagement-Student-Assistant_JR0001008": {
      "title": "Annual Giving & Gift Planning Engagement Student Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nDepartment: OSU Foundation Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: A Resume A Cover Letter For additional information please contact: Jason Thomas at Jason.thomas@osufoundation.org We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status.   OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire.   Note: All job offers are contingent upon Human Resources final approval Job Description: This recruitment will be used to fill one part-time (a maximum of 24 hours per week) Annual Giving & Gift Planning Engagement Student Assistant for the OSU Foundation at Oregon State University (OSU). The Oregon State University Foundation is seeking a student to join the Annual Giving and Gift Planning teams. Reporting jointly to the Senior Director of Annual Giving Programs and the Assistant Vice President of Gift Planning, this student worker will play a key role in supporting donor engagement, fundraising, stewardship, research, and marketing efforts across both programs. Responsibilities include assisting with donor outreach, stewardship communications, legacy donor engagement, student philanthropy initiatives, prospect research, database management, and campaign support, including Dam Proud Day and OSU Legacy Society activities. This position offers a unique opportunity to gain hands-on experience in nonprofit advancement while developing professional skills in communications, fundraising, donor relations, research, and data analysis. The student worker will contribute meaningfully to the culture of philanthropy at Oregon State University while gaining exposure to both annual and planned giving strategies. Position Duties: Promote philanthropy through student and donor engagement, stewardship calls, surveys, and outreach activities. Support Dam Proud Day, OSU Legacy Society, and other fundraising initiatives through event logistics, communications, and outreach. Thank donors, share impact stories, gather feedback, and assist with legacy donor engagement. Conduct market, donor, and prospect research to support fundraising and engagement strategies. Assist with donor cultivation efforts, including research, outreach preparation, and stewardship activities. Support the creation and editing of marketing, stewardship, and donor communications. Maintain donor records through data entry, contact reports, coding updates, and honor roll maintenance. Shadow advancement professionals and gain exposure to annual giving, gift planning, and donor stewardship. Provide general administrative support for the Annual Giving and Gift Planning teams. Perform other duties and special projects as assigned. Transferable Skill Development OSU is committed to ensuring students are prepared for success after graduation through intentional skill development as student employees. The competencies students develop while working at OSU are defined by the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) as the essential skills employers seek in their hires. In this position, students learn and build vital career-readiness skills in the primary areas below:   Communication, Critical Thinking, Teamwork, Technology, Leadership Qualifications: Full Employment Eligibility Requirements can be found here:   https://hr.oregonstate.edu/student-employment-manual/500-employment-eligibility-requirements Must be academically enrolled in a high school, community college, or university and pursuing a program or course of study Must meet Academic Standing Requirements; students on academic suspension are not eligible for employment Must meet the applicable minimal enrollment standard High School student: Regularly enrolled in a high school or participating in a home-schooling program Undergraduate and post-baccalaureate student: 6 credit hours per term Undergraduate international student: 12 credit hours per term* Graduate student officially admitted to Graduate School: 5 credit hours per term Graduate international student officially admitted to Graduate School: 9 credit hours per term* *International students may be allowed to carry fewer hours than specified above and still be considered “full-time” by the United States Citizenship and Immigration Services ( USCIS ). A reduced course load is approved by the   Office of International Services   ( OIS ), and must be provided to the Student Employment Center. Required Qualifications: Strong computer skills, including proficiency with Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, Teams, PowerPoint) and experience with databases or CRM systems.  Ability to research information through multiple electronic and paper files.  Strong organizational, oral and interpersonal skills and eye for detail.  Excellent interpersonal skills and ability to create strong professional relationships with colleagues at the OSU Foundation, OSU Alumni Association, and OSU. Strategic, hardworking, and able to work with a high degree of flexibility in a highly collaborative, fast-paced, goal-oriented environment. Ability to apply creative and entrepreneurial thinking while using sound judgment. Knowledge of appropriate research techniques and methods. Demonstrated sound judgment and high integrity, especially when handling confidential information.  Customer service orientation and a positive, proactive attitude.  Working Conditions/Schedule: This position will be based in Corvallis, Oregon and will work out of the OSU Foundation Corvallis office. The Foundation offers a program called Core Work Days, a hybrid approach combining remote and in-office work days. Unless traveling for work,  Foundation employees are in office on Tuesday, Wednesday and Thursday, and work remotely, if preferred, on Monday and Friday. This is a part-time position working up to 15-20 hours per week. Salary Range: Anticipated Start Date: 2026-09-21 Anticipated End Date:"
    },
    "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Guest-Experience-Associate_JR0000384": {
      "title": "Guest Experience Associate",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nDepartment: Patricia Valian Reser Center for the Creative Arts Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: A Resume A Cover Letter For additional information please contact: Tanner Buffy at Tanner.Buffy@oregonstate.edu Note for current OSU student employees: If you already have an active Workday profile, you must log in to Workday and apply through your employee account.  Please do not apply through the external career site, as this may prevent your application from being processed correctly. We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. This position requires driving a university vehicle or a personal vehicle on behalf of the University; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a Motor Vehicle History Check, possess and maintain a current, valid driver's license in their state of residence, be determined to be position qualified and self-report convictions (as per Voluntary and Compulsory Driver Standards OSU Standard 125-155-0200) as per OSU Standard 576-056-0000 et seq.   OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire.   Note: All job offers are contingent upon Human Resources final approval Job Description: This recruitment will be used to fill two part-time (a maximum of 24 hours per week) Guest Experience Associate positions for the Patricia Valian Reser Center for the Creative Arts (PRAx) at Oregon State University (OSU). The Undergraduate Student Outreach Assistant performs a variety of work related to outreach programs, including assistance at camps, youth programs, nutrition and education programs, and physical activity courses. Guest Experience Associates will help with event setup, ticket scanning, ushering, housekeeping, and support the Box Office and Guest Experience Manager and Front of House Coordinator with on and off-campus events and will be assigned where needed on any given day. Guest Experience Associates will be familiar with the current and upcoming events at PRAx, the performing and gallery spaces, policies, and will display a high level of customer service. Guest Experience Associates will be required to learn and follow the safety policies and procedures of PRAx. The position requires a demonstrated high level of discretion and sense of appropriateness, ability to maintain a calm and professional demeanor when working in stressful situations, as well as excellent communication and customer service skills. Guest Experience Associates are expected to use good judgement, to conduct themselves professionally while at work, to follow the guidelines for proper work attire, and to be punctual and reliable. Position Duties: Welcome, greet guests, and scan/verify tickets from event attendees. Politely direct and escort guests to their seats and/or venue entrances. Provide wayfinding of facilities and spaces at PRAx. Assist with crowd control and security. Calmly assists with disputes regarding tickets and seats. Attend staff meetings, pre-event meetings and other trainings as required by management. Visually sweep and tidy public spaces to check for potential safety issues, lost and found items, and cleanliness. Have knowledge and follow the proper procedures for assisting patrons with disabilities. Demonstrate knowledge of all spaces within PRAx and understand the evacuation procedures from all points within PRAx. Be punctual, work successfully, and communicate professionally with guests and staff. Other duties as assigned Transferable Skill Development OSU is committed to ensuring students are prepared for success after graduation through intentional skill development as student employees. The competencies students develop while working at OSU are defined by the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) as the essential skills employers seek in their hires. In this position, students learn and build vital career-readiness skills in the primary areas below:   Communication, Teamwork, Professionalism, Equity & Inclusion Qualifications: Full Employment Eligibility Requirements can be found here:   https://hr.oregonstate.edu/student-employment-manual/500-employment-eligibility-requirements Must be academically enrolled in a high school, community college, or university and pursuing a program or course of study Must meet Academic Standing Requirements; students on academic suspension are not eligible for employment Must meet the applicable minimal enrollment standard High School student: Regularly enrolled in a high school or participating in a home-schooling program Undergraduate and post-baccalaureate student: 6 credit hours per term Undergraduate international student: 12 credit hours per term* Graduate student officially admitted to Graduate School: 5 credit hours per term Graduate international student officially admitted to Graduate School: 9 credit hours per term* *International students may be allowed to carry fewer hours than specified above and still be considered “full-time” by the United States Citizenship and Immigration Services ( USCIS ). A reduced course load is approved by the   Office of International Services   ( OIS ), and must be provided to the Student Employment Center. Required Qualifications: Prior customer service experience. Ability to prove strong attention to detail. Ability to prove punctuality and reliability. Interest in performing arts, live events, music or technical theatre. Willingness to learn new skills and follow directions. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Ability to communicate effectively across different forms (radio, comms, email, etc) Ability to follow safety guidelines. Comfortable with moderate physical activity, including lifting up to 50 lbs. Additional Required Qualifications: This position requires driving a university vehicle or a personal vehicle on behalf of the University; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a Motor Vehicle History Check, possess and maintain a current, valid driver's license in their state of residence, be determined to be position qualified and self-report convictions (as per Voluntary and Compulsory Driver Standards OSU Standard 125-155-0200) as per OSU Standard 576-056-0000 et seq. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with theatre, concerts, or event production. Previous successful experience working in events, live performance, customer service, or hospitality. CPR certification. Working Conditions/Schedule: Work Conditions/Work Schedule: · Hours are based on the needs of events. Therefore, the schedule is variable and there is not a set number of hours guaranteed each week. · Must be able to work flexible hours, including weekdays, evenings, and weekends, depending on event needs. · Work is performed in theatres, studios, and other performance venues. · May involve standing for long periods, working in dim lighting and/or noisy environments, and working in confined and/or crowded areas. · Possible exposure to weather or outdoor conditions. · Potential driving and possible travel to work at events offsite. Ability to drive is preferred. · Preference given to those who can work 10-24 hours a week. This position will require flexible weekday, evening, and weekend work. Salary Range: 15.55-22.00 Anticipated Start Date: 2026-09-01 Anticipated End Date:"
    },
