    "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/KidSpirit-Swim-Instructor-School-Year-2026-2027_JR0000641": {
      "title": "KidSpirit Swim Instructor School Year 2026-2027",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nDepartment: KidSpirit Extension and Engagement Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: A Resume For additional information please contact: kidspirit@oregonstate.edu In addition to applying to the OSU job website portal please go to KidSpirit website to join our team and apply to KidSpirit. https://kidspirit.oregonstate.edu/employment We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status.   This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a Criminal History Check and be determined to be position qualified as per OSU Standard 576-055-0000 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in Youth Programs may have additional Criminal History Checks every 2 years.   OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire.   Note: All job offers are contingent upon Human Resources final approval Job Description: This recruitment will be used to fill 30 part-time (a maximum of 24 hours per week) Swim Instructor for the KidSpirit Youth Organization at Oregon State University (OSU). The Youth Program Instructor is responsible for delivering high‑quality instruction to youth while fostering a safe, supportive, and growth‑oriented environment. The position requires strong communication, critical thinking, teamwork, and a commitment to ongoing professional development. Responsibilities include lesson planning, safety response, equipment management, program promotion, and effective collaboration with staff, families, and supervisors. WSI certification preferred or ability to participate in WSI training. Swim Lesson Experience / Training Preferred or High Level of Swim Experience Join Our Team | OSU–KidSpirit | Extension and Engagement | Oregon State University Position Duties: Create and maintain an instructional environment that prioritizes skill mastery, emotional safety, and positive youth development. Plan, prepare, and implement age-appropriate lessons and activities that support participant growth and engagement. Use observation, critical thinking, and feedback strategies to evaluate participants and support staff performance. Monitor participant safety always and administer first aid when necessary. Initiate emergency action procedures appropriately and calmly. Attend required orientation sessions, program meetings, and in‑service training. Check out, request, and properly use equipment and supplies for activities. Transferable Skill Development OSU is committed to ensuring students are prepared for success after graduation through intentional skill development as student employees. The competencies students develop while working at OSU are defined by the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) as the essential skills employers seek in their hires. In this position, students learn and build vital career-readiness skills in the primary areas below:   Communication, Critical Thinking, Teamwork, Professionalism Qualifications: Full Employment Eligibility Requirements can be found here:   https://hr.oregonstate.edu/student-employment-manual/500-employment-eligibility-requirements Must be academically enrolled in a high school, community college, or university and pursuing a program or course of study Must meet Academic Standing Requirements; students on academic suspension are not eligible for employment Must meet the applicable minimal enrollment standard High School student: Regularly enrolled in a high school or participating in a home-schooling program Undergraduate and post-baccalaureate student: 6 credit hours per term Undergraduate international student: 12 credit hours per term* Graduate student officially admitted to Graduate School: 5 credit hours per term Graduate international student officially admitted to Graduate School: 9 credit hours per term* *International students may be allowed to carry fewer hours than specified above and still be considered “full-time” by the United States Citizenship and Immigration Services ( USCIS ). A reduced course load is approved by the   Office of International Services   ( OIS ), and must be provided to the Student Employment Center. Required Qualifications: Current, valid First Aid certification by the start of programming. Recognizing and Reporting Child Abuse and Neglect (RRCAN) certification by start of programming. Introduction to Child Care Health & Safety certification by start of programming. Fundamentals of Learning. Additional Required Qualifications: This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a Criminal History Check and be determined to be position qualified as per OSU Standard 576-055-0000 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in Youth Programs may have additional Criminal History Checks every 2 years. Working Conditions/Schedule: • On campus pools, Langton and Women Building. • Afternoons Monday thru Friday, weekdays may vary like Tuesday, Thursday, Friday. Weekends, Saturday and Sunday. • Can possibly accommodate working one day on the weekend, Saturday or Sunday. • KidSpirit swim lessons run both Saturday and Sunday. Salary Range: Anticipated Start Date: 2026-08-31 Anticipated End Date:"
    },
    "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Student-Project-Assistant_JR0001004": {
      "title": "Student Project Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nDepartment: Fisheries, Wildlife, and Conservation Sciences Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: A 1-page (or less) cover letter and resume that specifically addresses required and desired qualifications listed in this post. For additional information please contact: Lauren Rice at lauren.rice@oregonstate.edu We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status.   OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire.   Note: All job offers are contingent upon Human Resources final approval Job Description: This recruitment will be used to fill two part-time (a maximum of 24 hours per week) Project Assistant positions for the Human Dimensions Lab in the Department of Fisheries, Wildlife, and Conservation Sciences at Oregon State University (OSU). The Human Dimensions Lab at Oregon State University is seeking two research assistants to provide technical and data entry support for a study on human wellbeing in the Puget Sound. The project assistants will input survey data into an Excel database, ensuring accuracy, consistency, and efficiency. They will work closely under the project lead, Lauren Rice, to develop strategies and expectations for their work. Position Duties Completion of human subjects training through the CITI Program Read literature relevant to the project Enter survey data using Microsoft Excel Develop strategies for issues that may arise during data entry Communicate often with project lead, including check-ins and deadlines Transferable Skill Development OSU is committed to ensuring students are prepared for success after graduation through intentional skill development as student employees. The competencies students develop while working at OSU are defined by the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) as the essential skills employers seek in their hires. In this position, students learn and build vital career-readiness skills in the primary areas below:   Communication, Teamwork, Professionalism, Career & Self Development Qualifications: Full Employment Eligibility Requirements can be found here:   https://hr.oregonstate.edu/student-employment-manual/500-employment-eligibility-requirements Must be academically enrolled in a high school, community college, or university and pursuing a program or course of study Must meet Academic Standing Requirements; students on academic suspension are not eligible for employment Must meet the applicable minimal enrollment standard High School student: Regularly enrolled in a high school or participating in a home-schooling program Undergraduate and post-baccalaureate student: 6 credit hours per term Undergraduate international student: 12 credit hours per term* Graduate student officially admitted to Graduate School: 5 credit hours per term Graduate international student officially admitted to Graduate School: 9 credit hours per term* *International students may be allowed to carry fewer hours than specified above and still be considered “full-time” by the United States Citizenship and Immigration Services ( USCIS ). A reduced course load is approved by the   Office of International Services   ( OIS ), and must be provided to the Student Employment Center. Required Able to complete high-quality work doing repetitive tasks Detail oriented and able to work independently but not shy to seek advice Comfortable with Microsoft or similar software products Able to follow confidentiality procedures and be committed to ethical research practices Undergraduate and graduate students welcome to apply Work study and non-work study eligible students welcome to apply On campus and Ecampus students welcome but must work on OSU, Corvallis campus Preferred Some experience with survey data Some experience with Microsoft Excel Some exposure to qualitative research methods Completion of IRB CITI human subjects training Working Conditions/Schedule: All work will be completed on a laptop computer indoors. Laptops and software are provided. Salary Range: 17 Anticipated Start Date: 2026-10-15 Anticipated End Date:"
    },
    "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Creative---Design-Services-Student-Team-Member_JR0000984-1": {
      "title": "Creative & Design Services Student Team Member",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 13 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nDepartment: Printing & Mailing Services Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: A Resume A Cover Letter A Porfolio For additional information please contact: Kent St Clair at kent.stclair@oregonstate.edu We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status.   This position requires driving a University vehicle or a personal vehicle on behalf of the University; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a Motor Vehicle History Check , possess and maintain a current, valid driver's license in their state of residence, be determined to be position qualified and self-report convictions (as per Voluntary and Compulsory Driver Standards OSU Standard 125-155-0200) as per OSU Standard 576-056-0000 et seq.   OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire.   Note: All job offers are contingent upon Human Resources final approval Job Description: This recruitment will be used to fill eight part-time (a maximum of 24 hours per week) Creative & Design Services Team Member position for the Printing and Mailing Services at Oregon State University (OSU). Marketing Services and Solutions DAM Creative team is looking for Creatives! (Student graphic designers, illustrators, animators, photographers, and video editors) to join our creative team. This position offers a unique opportunity for students to: Create visually compelling designs for a wide range of marketing materials, including websites, posters, social media graphics, and more. Work closely with team members to bring fresh ideas to life. Use the latest design tools and technologies to create high-quality, impactful visual content. Contribute to a culture of creativity and collaboration, delivering designs that exceed expectations. Why Join Us? Gain real-world experience working with university departments and clients across OSU. Build a strong portfolio with creative projects that stand out in the industry. Work in a fast-paced, collaborative environment where your ideas are valued and your growth is encouraged. Access cutting-edge tools and technologies to sharpen your design skills. Position Duties Graphic Designers: Design and produce marketing materials such as flyers, posters, banners, digital ads, impact reports As a part of the DAM Creative team, you will work collaboratively to ensure that all designs meet the program’s needs and brand standards. Contribute to the visual design aspects of DAM Creative web presence and promotional campaign Experience with Adobe Creative Suite Photographers: Capture high-quality photographs of programs, events, and activities, ensuring coverage of key moments and features. Edit, process, and prepare photos for marketing materials, social media, and web content. Collaborate with graphic designers to ensure that photos are integrated effectively (in a way that enhances the overall design and message) into various design projects. Video Editors: Develop and edit video content highlighting programs, events, and promotional efforts. Assist in the planning, filming, and producing video projects, ensuring content is engaging Work with the team to produce videos that effectively tell the story of DAM Creatives impact and offerings. Transferable Skill Development OSU is committed to ensuring students are prepared for success after graduation through intentional skill development as student employees. The competencies students develop while working at OSU are defined by the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) as the essential skills employers seek in their hires. In this position, students learn and build vital career-readiness skills in the primary areas below:   Communication, Teamwork, Technology Career & Self Development Qualifications: Full Employment Eligibility Requirements can be found here:   https://hr.oregonstate.edu/student-employment-manual/500-employment-eligibility-requirement Must be academically enrolled in a high school, community college, or university and pursuing a program or course of study Must meet Academic Standing Requirements; students on academic suspension are not eligible for employment Must meet the applicable minimal enrollment standard High School student: Regularly enrolled in a high school or participating in a home-schooling program Undergraduate and post-baccalaureate student: 6 credit hours per term Undergraduate international student: 12 credit hours per term* Graduate student officially admitted to Graduate School: 5 credit hours per term Graduate international student officially admitted to Graduate School: 9 credit hours per term* *International students may be allowed to carry fewer hours than specified above and still be considered “full-time” by the United States Citizenship and Immigration Services ( USCIS ). A reduced course load is approved by the   Office of International Services   ( OIS ), and must be provided to the Student Employment Center. Required This position requires driving a University vehicle or a personal vehicle on behalf of the University; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a Motor Vehicle History Check , possess and maintain a current, valid driver's license in their state of residence, be determined to be position qualified and self-report convictions (as per Voluntary and Compulsory Driver Standards OSU Standard 125-155-0200) as per OSU Standard 576-056-0000 et seq. Preferred Working towards a degree in Graphic Design, Photography, Videography, Visual Arts, Media Studies, or a related field Experience in the field are encouraged to apply Demonstrated experience in graphic design, photography, or video editing, with a strong portfolio of previous work Experienced in Adobe Creative Suite (InDesign, Photoshop, Illustrator, Premiere Pro, etc.), and other relevant multimedia design and editing tools (such as Lightroom, Final Cut Pro, or After Effects) Excellent communication and teamwork skills, proactive attitude and a willingness to take on multiple projects Ability to work flexibly Opportunity to work creatively and solve complex problems with visual solutions, A demonstrable commitment to promoting and enhancing diversity Working Conditions/Schedule: Salary Range: Anticipated Start Date: 2026-10-23 Anticipated End Date:"
    },
    "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Beaver-Classic-Retail-Manager_JR0000232": {
      "title": "Beaver Classic Retail Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-01\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nDepartment: Food Science & Technology Special Instructions to Applicants: The closing date has been extended in order to expand the original applicant pool. To ensure full consideration, applications must be received by August 16, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted after the full consideration date, until a sufficient applicant pool has been achieved or the position is filled. The closing date is subject to change without notice to applicants. When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents:   1) A resume/CV; and   2) A cover letter indicating how your education, training, and professional experience have prepared you for this position.   Starting salary will be commensurate with skills, education, and experience.   For additional information please contact: Lisbeth Goddik lisbeth.goddik@oregonstate.edu Job Summary: The Department of Food Science & Technology is seeking a Beaver Classic Retail Manager. This is a full-time (1.00 FTE), 12-month, professional faculty position. Join the Beaver Classic™ program within Oregon State University's Department of Food Science and Technology and play a leadership role in a unique, student-centered retail enterprise that connects food production, product innovation, and hands-on learning. The Beaver Classic Retail Manager oversees sales and operations across the Beaver Classic Market, food truck, farmers markets, e-commerce, and community events while working closely with faculty, staff, and production teams to bring high-quality, student-made products to consumers. This position offers the opportunity to shape Beaver Classic retail strategy, expand product offerings, and strengthen community engagement while supporting OSU's mission of teaching, research, and outreach. As part of the Department of Food Science and Technology , this position helps provide meaningful experiential learning opportunities for students while managing a growing and highly visible Beaver Classic retail program. The role combines business operations, marketing, financial management, and customer engagement in a collaborative environment dedicated to innovation, food science education, and excellence in product development and production. Learn more about Beaver Classic and the Department of Food Science and Technology at https://beaverclassic.com/ and https://foodsci.oregonstate.edu/ Key Responsibilities: Management of Beaver Classic Market, Food Truck, Events, and Online Sales Provide leadership and oversight for Beaver Classic retail operations, including the Beaver Classic Market, Food Truck, catering and special events, and online sales. Manage daily operations, sales activities, merchandising, product fulfillment, and customer service to ensure a high-quality customer experience and achievement of revenue goals. Strategic Planning and Partnership Development Develop, implement, and evaluate strategic plans that support Beaver Classic retail growth, profitability, and brand awareness. Administrative Management Evaluate and improve operational procedures, policies, training materials, and business practices to ensure efficient, customer-focused operations. Service Serve on department, college, and university committees and participate in activities that contribute to the success of the Department of Food Science and Technology, the College of Agricultural Sciences, and Oregon State University. Qualifications: Required Qualifications: Associate degree in food service management, nutritional care, food science, business, or related field AND four years of food service supervisory experience; OR a bachelor’s degree with a major course work in restaurant or hotel management, food science, business, or a closely related field and one year of food service supervisory experience. Demonstrated experience in food safety including microbial and allergen controls. Experience managing budgets, calculating Cost of Goods Sold (COGS), and profit and loss accounting. Experience supervising and mentoring entry-level employees and/or students. Ability to work irregular hours including evenings and weekends, including communication outside of working hours. For example, may include Saturday Farmers Market, and College of Agricultural Sciences special events. Ability to lift and carry items weighing up to 50 lbs, and push/pull items weighing 50-100 lbs. Must acquire a Oregon Food Handler’s license within 15 days of hire, and maintain license by renewing every 3 years. Commitment to promoting and enhancing inclusive excellence. This position requires driving a university vehicle or a personal vehicle on behalf of the university; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a motor vehicle history check, possess and maintain a current, valid driver's license in their state of residence, be determined to be position qualified and self-report convictions as per University Policy 05-030. This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a criminal history check and be determined to be position qualified as per University Standard: 05-010 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in youth programs may have additional criminal history checks every 24 months.   Preferred Qualifications: Strong preference for a bachelor’s degree with a major course work in restaurant or hotel management or a closely related field. Demonstrated effective customer relations, interpersonal skills, and communication. Able to prioritize and complete assigned multiple tasks and responsibilities promptly. Hazard Analysis and Critical Control Points (HACCP) training. Experience running a small business. Working Conditions/Schedule: Working Conditions/Work Schedule: Work environment includes working in various environments including office, food truck in outdoor environment for events, retail store, storage and freezer or refrigerated areas, and other environments as needed. Position requires working some irregular hours including evenings and weekends. Position requires travel to event locations with food truck or other vehicle. Event venues include on and off campus college or university events, local farmers markets, festivals/fairs, and others. Position will lift and carry items weighing up to 50 lbs, push/pull items weighing 50-100 lbs, will require climbing stairs and repetitive motions. Salary Range: $55,000 - $67,000 Anticipated Start Date: 2026-11-02 Anticipated End Date: We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire. OSU is a fair chance employer committed to inclusive hiring. We encourage applications from candidates who bring a wide range of lived experience including involvement with the justice system. If this position has “critical or security-sensitive” responsibilities and/or driving duties and you are selected as a finalist, your initial job offer will be contingent upon the results of a job-related pre-employment check (such as a background check, motor vehicle history check, sexual misconduct reference check, etc.). Background check results do not automatically disqualify a candidate. Take a look at our Background Checks website including the for candidates section for more details. If you have questions or concerns about the pre-employment check, please contact OSU’s Employee and Labor Relations team at employee.relations@oregonstate.edu ."
    },
