    "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/BA-270-Teaching-Assistant_JR0000751": {
      "title": "BA 270 Teaching Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nDepartment: College of Business School of Accounting, Finance, and Information Systems Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: A Resume A Cover Letter For additional information please contact: Venkataramani Raja at VT.Raja@bus.oregonstate.edu We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status.   This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a Criminal History Check and be determined to be position qualified as per OSU Standard 576-055-0000 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in Youth Programs may have additional Criminal History Checks every 2 years.   OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire.   Note: All job offers are contingent upon Human Resources final approval Job Description: This recruitment will be used to fill 1 part-time (a maximum of 24 hours per week) Teaching Assistant position for the College of Business at Oregon State University (OSU). This is a part-time Teaching Assistant (TA) position for some sections of the BA270 course. The TA will have access to confidential data (e.g., Personally Identifiable Information).  Hence, they must have high integrity, strong work ethics, and must abide by OSU and FERPA rules. Depending on their availability, candidate can work for a minimum of five hours per week, and a maximum of 20 hours per week. A majority of the TA work can be done remotely. Depending on candidate’s availability and instructor/student needs, the TA work may involve lab demos, meeting with instructor, conducting help sessions, grading, editing content on the course Canvas site, communicating with instructor/students, and exam proctoring. Pay rate for this position is $16.55 per hour. Position Duties: The successful candidate will meet with instructor as needed and help with some activities such as: Reviewing and editing content on Canvas course site Grading and data entry Transcribing audio recordings of lectures Conducting IT lab help sessions (e.g., basic Microsoft Visio) The successful candidate is expected to: Work one-on-one with students seeking academic help relating to BA270 (this may involve in-person and virtual meetings with students) Have good interpersonal, listening, verbal and written communication skills Be organized and have good time management skills Identify and help process any academic integrity violations that may occur in the BA270 course. Transferable Skill Development OSU is committed to ensuring students are prepared for success after graduation through intentional skill development as student employees. The competencies students develop while working at OSU are defined by the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) as the essential skills employers seek in their hires. In this position, students learn and build vital career-readiness skills in the primary areas below:   Communication, Critical Thinking, Professionalism Qualifications: Full Employment Eligibility Requirements can be found here:   https://hr.oregonstate.edu/student-employment-manual/500-employment-eligibility-requirements Must be academically enrolled in a high school, community college, or university and pursuing a program or course of study Must meet Academic Standing Requirements; students on academic suspension are not eligible for employment Must meet the applicable minimal enrollment standard High School student: Regularly enrolled in a high school or participating in a home-schooling program Undergraduate and post-baccalaureate student: 6 credit hours per term Undergraduate international student: 12 credit hours per term* Graduate student officially admitted to Graduate School: 5 credit hours per term Graduate international student officially admitted to Graduate School: 9 credit hours per term* *International students may be allowed to carry fewer hours than specified above and still be considered “full-time” by the United States Citizenship and Immigration Services ( USCIS ). A reduced course load is approved by the   Office of International Services   ( OIS) and must be provided to the Student Employment Center. Required Qualifications: Applicants must have successfully completed BA 270 (Business Process Management) course at Oregon State University Applicants must be comfortable using and teaching MS Visio, MS Dynamics and MS Office software as they relate to BA 270 Applicants must be interested in helping students with BA 270 related content. Additional Required Qualifications: This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a Criminal History Check and be determined to be position qualified as per OSU Standard 576-055-0000 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in Youth Programs may have additional Criminal History Checks every 2 years. Preferred Qualifications: Preference will be given to applicants with a service mindset who are genuinely interested in helping students with BA 270 related content Professionalism would be a preferred key attribute Applicants must have successfully completed BA270 (Business Process Management) course at Oregon State University with a grade of B+ or higher Working Conditions/Schedule: As the course may be an e-campus course, the job may require TAs to work and help students outside regular business hours. However, there is ample flexibility in selecting the hours during which the TA would prefer to work each week. The position allows for much variation in the hours selected each week. Typically, access to training by outgoing TA who is graduating is available for newly hired TA. Salary Range: Anticipated Start Date: 2026-09-17 Anticipated End Date:"
    },
    "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/DSGN-464-Student-Teaching-Assistant_JR0000889": {
      "title": "DSGN 464 Student Teaching Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nDepartment: College of Business – School of Marketing, Analytics, and Design Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: ●        A Resume ●        A Cover Letter For additional information please contact: Marilyn Read at Marilyn.Read@oregonstate.edu This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a Criminal History Check and be determined to be position qualified as per OSU Standard 576-055-0000 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in Youth Programs may have additional Criminal History Checks every 2 years. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire.   Note: All job offers are contingent upon Human Resources final approval Job Description: This recruitment will be used to fill 1 part-time (a maximum of 24 hours per week) student job for the College of Business at Oregon State University (OSU). Assist instructor with DSGN 464 - History of Interiors course during class time, and Hold 1 office hour each week for students, in person or virtual. Pay rate for this position is $16.55 per hour.   Position Duties Assist with creating weekly writing assignments for in-class discussion Assist with facilitating discussions with small groups of students during class time Transferable Skill Development OSU is committed to ensuring students are prepared for success after graduation through intentional skill development as student employees. The competencies students develop while working at OSU are defined by the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) as the essential skills employers seek in their hires. In this position, students learn and build vital career-readiness skills in the primary areas below:   Communication, Teamwork, Career & Self Development Qualifications: Full Employment Eligibility Requirements can be found here:   https://hr.oregonstate.edu/student-employment-manual/500-employment-eligibility-requirements Must be academically enrolled in a high school, community college, or university and pursuing a program or course of study Must meet Academic Standing Requirements; students on academic suspension are not eligible for employment Must meet the applicable minimal enrollment standard High School student: Regularly enrolled in a high school or participating in a home-schooling program Undergraduate and post-baccalaureate student: 6 credit hours per term Undergraduate international student: 12 credit hours per term* Graduate student officially admitted to Graduate School: 5 credit hours per term Graduate international student officially admitted to Graduate School: 9 credit hours per term* *International students may be allowed to carry fewer hours than specified above and still be considered “full-time” by the United States Citizenship and Immigration Services ( USCIS ). A reduced course load is approved by the   Office of International Services   ( OIS ), and must be provided to the Student Employment Center. Required: Applicants have completed the DSGN 464 - History of Interiors course This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a Criminal History Check and be determined to be position qualified as per OSU Standard 576-055-0000 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in Youth Programs may have additional Criminal History Checks every 2 years. Preferred: Applicants have completed additional art history courses Working Conditions/Schedule: - 5 hours/ week - Meet during class time TR 12:00-1:20 Salary Range: Anticipated Start Date: 2026-09-23 Anticipated End Date:"
