    "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/BA-211-Student-Teaching-Assistant_JR0000925": {
      "title": "BA 211 Student Teaching Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nDepartment: College of Business – School of Accounting, Finance, and Information Systems Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: A Resume A Cover Letter For additional information please contact: Ashlee Burke at ashlee.burke@oregonstate.ed u We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a Criminal History Check and be determined to be position qualified as per OSU Standard 576-055-0000 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in Youth Programs may have additional Criminal History Checks every 2 years. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire.   Note: All job offers are contingent upon Human Resources final approval Job Description: This recruitment will be used to fill 2 part-time (a maximum of 10 hours per week) BA 211 Teaching Assistant positions for the College of Business at Oregon State University (OSU). These are TA position for all of the BA 211 courses, and potentially other accounting courses should the need arise, for the academic year. Successful candidates can expect to: Assist in grading Assis in grade entry Provide tutoring and/or host office hours Assist with exam proctoring Successful candidate will be expected to understand the course material, be flexible, and have good listening skills with the ability to assist students in the learning of course material.  Pay rate for this position is $16.55 per hour. Position Duties The successful candidate is expected to assist with tasks such as grading, provide tutoring, help with Canvas management, and help with exam proctoring. Transferable Skill Development OSU is committed to ensuring students are prepared for success after graduation through intentional skill development as student employees. The competencies students develop while working at OSU are defined by the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) as the essential skills employers seek in their hires. In this position, students learn and build vital career-readiness skills in the primary areas below:   Communication, Professionalism, Career & Self Development Qualifications: Full Employment Eligibility Requirements can be found here:   https://hr.oregonstate.edu/student-employment-manual/500-employment-eligibility-requirements Must be academically enrolled in a high school, community college, or university and pursuing a program or course of study Must meet Academic Standing Requirements; students on academic suspension are not eligible for employment Must meet the applicable minimal enrollment standard High School student: Regularly enrolled in a high school or participating in a home-schooling program Undergraduate and post-baccalaureate student: 6 credit hours per term Undergraduate international student: 12 credit hours per term* Graduate student officially admitted to Graduate School: 5 credit hours per term Graduate international student officially admitted to Graduate School: 9 credit hours per term* *International students may be allowed to carry fewer hours than specified above and still be considered “full-time” by the United States Citizenship and Immigration Services ( USCIS ). A reduced course load is approved by the   Office of International Services   ( OIS ), and must be provided to the Student Employment Center. Required: Applicants must have successfully completed BA 211 at Oregon State University with a B or higher. This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a Criminal History Check and be determined to be position qualified as per OSU Standard 576-055-0000 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in Youth Programs may have additional Criminal History Checks every 2 years. Preferred: Preference is for students who have successfully completed the Intermediate Accounting Series (ACTG317/318/319) with a B or higher. Working Conditions/Schedule: The successful candidate can work around their class schedule but should be available to assist proctoring exams and grading during specific weeks. Salary Range: Anticipated Start Date: 2026-09-21 Anticipated End Date:"
    },
    "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Student-Support-Technology--SST-_JR0000891": {
      "title": "Student Support Technology (SST)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nDepartment: College of Business – Information Systems Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: ●        A Resume ●        A Cover Letter For additional information please contact: Alan Sprague at alan.sprague@oregonstate.edu We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a Criminal History Check and be determined to be position qualified as per OSU Standard 576-055-0000 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in Youth Programs may have additional Criminal History Checks every 2 years. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire.   Note: All job offers are contingent upon Human Resources final approval Job Description: This recruitment will be used to fill four part-time (a maximum of 24 hours per week) Student Support Technology (SST) position for the College of Business at Oregon State University (OSU). Pay rate for this position is 16.80 per hour. Position Duties Customer Service, Troubleshooting, and Equipment Maintenance Responding to walk-in, phone, and email questions about the computer lab Maintaining printers Cleaning computer labs and common areas Maintaining communication between Level 2 Student Support Technicians and full-time employees. Making and monitoring tickets within our ticketing system (Service Now). Opening and closing facilities Limited facilities maintenance Transferable Skill Development OSU is committed to ensuring students are prepared for success after graduation through intentional skill development as student employees. The competencies students develop while working at OSU are defined by the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) as the essential skills employers seek in their hires. In this position, students learn and build vital career-readiness skills in the primary areas below:   Critical Thinking, Technology, Professionalism,Career & Self Development Qualifications: Full Employment Eligibility Requirements can be found here:   https://hr.oregonstate.edu/student-employment-manual/500-employment-eligibility-requirements Must be academically enrolled in a high school, community college, or university and pursuing a program or course of study Must meet Academic Standing Requirements; students on academic suspension are not eligible for employment Must meet the applicable minimal enrollment standard High School student: Regularly enrolled in a high school or participating in a home-schooling program Undergraduate and post-baccalaureate student: 6 credit hours per term Undergraduate international student: 12 credit hours per term* Graduate student officially admitted to Graduate School: 5 credit hours per term Graduate international student officially admitted to Graduate School: 9 credit hours per term* *International students may be allowed to carry fewer hours than specified above and still be considered “full-time” by the United States Citizenship and Immigration Services ( USCIS ). A reduced course load is approved by the   Office of International Services   ( OIS ), and must be provided to the Student Employment Center. Required: Interpersonal communication skills, including phone etiquette Professional and courteous demeanor Desire to provide outstanding customer service Ability to work independently and learn quickly Self-motivated This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a Criminal History Check and be determined to be position qualified as per OSU Standard 576-055-0000 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in Youth Programs may have additional Criminal History Checks every 2 years. Preferred: Experience with Microsoft Office 365 Demonstrated knowledge of Windows 11 Familiarity with Active Directory, DNS, DHCP, and networking basics A demonstrable commitment to promoting and enhancing diversity Working Conditions/Schedule: - Schedules are fixed by term, flexible with class schedules, and are 10-24 hours per week. - Available to work Monday through Friday 7 AM – 10 PM, Saturday 8 AM – 6 PM, and Sunday 12 PM – 8 PM. - Hours that are outside business hours may be expected depending on availability. Salary Range: Anticipated Start Date: 2026-10-05 Anticipated End Date:"
    },
    "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Student-Teaching-Assistant-for-BA275---Foundations-of-Statistical-Inference_JR0000933": {
      "title": "Student Teaching Assistant for BA275 – Foundations of Statistical Inference",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nDepartment: College of Business – School of Management, Entrepreneurship & Supply Chain Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: ●        A Resume ●        A Brief Cover Letter For additional information please contact: Katie Jager at katie.jager@oregonstate.edu We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status.   This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a Criminal History Check and be determined to be position qualified as per OSU Standard 576-055-0000 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in Youth Programs may have additional Criminal History Checks every 2 years. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire.   Note: All job offers are contingent upon Human Resources final approval Job Description: This recruitment will be used to fill 1 part-time (a maximum of 24 hours per week) student job for the College of Business at Oregon State University (OSU). Join us in empowering students to excel in their understanding of statistics for business! We are seeking a dedicated and knowledgeable Teaching Assistant (TA) for BA275  - Foundations of Statistical Inference for the upcoming academic year (2024-2025). As a TA, you will play a vital role in supporting students' learning and comprehension of statistical concepts. This position offers an excellent opportunity to enhance your leadership and communication skills, deepen your understanding of quantitative methods used in business, and contribute to the academic success of students in the College of Business. Pay rate for this position is $16.55 per hour. Position Duties The following duties are expected to take about 4 – 8 hours per week. Assist the instructor in proctoring exams on campus. Hold regular office hours to provide additional support and guidance to students. Grade weekly assignments and/or discussion boards online with feedback. Foster a positive and inclusive learning environment for all students. Respond promptly to student inquiries and concerns via email or in-person. Transferable Skill Development OSU is committed to ensuring students are prepared for success after graduation through intentional skill development as student employees. The competencies students develop while working at OSU are defined by the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) as the essential skills employers seek in their hires. In this position, students learn and build vital career-readiness skills in the primary areas below:   Communication, Critical Thinking, Professionalism Qualifications: Full Employment Eligibility Requirements can be found here:   https://hr.oregonstate.edu/student-employment-manual/500-employment-eligibility-requirements Must be academically enrolled in a high school, community college, or university and pursuing a program or course of study Must meet Academic Standing Requirements; students on academic suspension are not eligible for employment Must meet the applicable minimal enrollment standard High School student: Regularly enrolled in a high school or participating in a home-schooling program Undergraduate and post-baccalaureate student: 6 credit hours per term Undergraduate international student: 12 credit hours per term* Graduate student officially admitted to Graduate School: 5 credit hours per term Graduate international student officially admitted to Graduate School: 9 credit hours per term* *International students may be allowed to carry fewer hours than specified above and still be considered “full-time” by the United States Citizenship and Immigration Services ( USCIS ). A reduced course load is approved by the   Office of International Services   ( OIS ), and must be provided to the Student Employment Center. Required: Must have completed at least one class in statistics with a minimum grade of B+. Demonstrated enthusiasm for statistics and a genuine desire to help others learn. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to complete tasks in a timely and organized manner. Perform basic functions in excel. This position is designated as a critical or security-sensitive position; therefore, the incumbent must successfully complete a Criminal History Check and be determined to be position qualified as per OSU Standard 576-055-0000 et seq. Incumbents are required to self-report convictions and those in Youth Programs may have additional Criminal History Checks every 2 years. Preferred: Taken BA275 with Katie Jager and has earned and A- or above. Currently a Business Analytics major or is earning a statistics minor Previous teaching or tutoring experience is preferred but not required. Working Conditions/Schedule: The TA position is for the duration of the 2026-2027 academic year starting Fall Term (some training may start prior to the end of spring term). Applicants must be available to work on campus during this time. Working schedule is 4-8 hours per week. Salary Range: Anticipated Start Date: 2026-09-21 Anticipated End Date:"
    },
