    "https://oregonstate.wd501.myworkdayjobs.com/OSU_Careers_Site/job/Corvallis-Main-Campus/Accessible-Formats-Student-Tech_JR0001124": {
      "title": "Accessible Formats Student Tech",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-15\nPosted: Posted Yesterday\nPart time\n\nDepartment: Library Special Instructions to Applicants: When applying you will be required to attach the following electronic documents: ●        A Resume ●        A Cover Letter For additional information please contact: Lucinda Amerman at Lucinda.amerman@oregonstate.edu We are an Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability, protected veteran, and other protected status. OSU will conduct a review of the National Sex Offender Public website prior to hire.   Note: All job offers are contingent upon Human Resources final approval Job Description: This recruitment will be used to fill one part-time (a maximum of 24 hours per week) Accessible Formats Student Tech position for the Valley Library at Oregon State University (OSU). Valley Library is seeking a student to remediate Word and PDF documents for increased accessibility (primarily screen reader accessibility) for 10 to 15 hours/week, starting as soon as availability allows. Work schedule is during regular business hours (M-F, 8-5). This position will re-format archival and current publications to set standards, author alternative text for images, and correct transcriptions and PDF structures. No prior experience necessary, all training provided. Position Duties In this position you will: Learn how to use specialized software to correct Optical Character Recognition (OCR) and PDF structures (Technology). Use AI tools to create effective and unbiased alternative text descriptions for complex images and Microsoft Word to edit documents to attain accessible standards (Equity & Inclusion, Critical Thinking) As skills develop over time, you will: Work with increased independence as you creatively resolve accessibility barriers in pdf documents (Critical Thinking, Equity & Inclusion) Learn advanced accessibility techniques for PDF remediation and complex graphics (Technology) Collaborate with OSULP employees on process improvements or additional projects (Teamwork) Transferable Skill Development OSU is committed to ensuring students are prepared for success after graduation through intentional skill development as student employees. The competencies students develop while working at OSU are defined by the National Association of Colleges and Employers (NACE) as the essential skills employers seek in their hires. In this position, students learn and build vital career-readiness skills in the primary areas below:   Critical Thinking, Teamwork, Technology, Equity & Inclusion Qualifications: Full Employment Eligibility Requirements can be found here:   https://hr.oregonstate.edu/student-employment-manual/500-employment-eligibility-requirements Must be academically enrolled in a high school, community college, or university and pursuing a program or course of study Must meet Academic Standing Requirements; students on academic suspension are not eligible for employment Must meet the applicable minimal enrollment standard High School student: Regularly enrolled in a high school or participating in a home-schooling program Undergraduate and post-baccalaureate student: 6 credit hours per term Undergraduate international student: 12 credit hours per term* Graduate student officially admitted to Graduate School: 5 credit hours per term Graduate international student officially admitted to Graduate School: 9 credit hours per term* *International students may be allowed to carry fewer hours than specified above and still be considered “full-time” by the United States Citizenship and Immigration Services ( USCIS ). A reduced course load is approved by the   Office of International Services   ( OIS ), and must be provided to the Student Employment Center. Required Basic knowledge of creating documents using a Word processor (Microsoft Word preferred) Basic knowledge of Microsoft Office and/or comparable Google tools (Excel/Sheets, Word/Docs) Strong attention to detail Ability to stay focused on tasks in an office environment Ability to follow precise instructions and ask clarifying questions as needed Effective communication skills Preferred Familiarity with STEM material A demonstrable commitment to promoting and enhancing diversity, equity, and inclusion Working Conditions/Schedule: Work Schedule: 10-15 hours per week Working Conditions: - Tasks will take place in an office environment, onsite only. - Shifts are normally scheduled for standard office hours, M-F, 8-5 Salary Range: Anticipated Start Date: 2026-10-16 Anticipated End Date:"
